{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "detector-guard",
  "description": "On every edit of an app detector, audit registration, labels and the three test tiers, and generate any missing test.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": ["apps/*/detectors/*.py"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A detector module under apps/zombie_subscriptions/detectors/ or apps/phantom_invoices/detectors/ was edited. First, if the edited file is __init__.py or utils.py, stop and do nothing: those two files are not detectors. Otherwise audit the edited detector and REPORT what you checked and every gap you find. Do not rewrite or refactor working detector code; only add missing tests.\n\nChecks (state PASS/GAP for each):\n1. Registration: the detector is registered with a namespaced name, prefix 'zs.' for apps/zombie_subscriptions and 'pi.' for apps/phantom_invoices, and it is discovered by auto_discover in the app's detectors/__init__.py. For phantom_invoices there is also an entry in LABELS in apps/phantom_invoices/detectors/__init__.py.\n2. Test module: apps/<app>/tests/ contains test_zs_<module>.py or test_pi_<module>.py (app prefix mandatory, see .kiro/steering/structure.md).\n3. Tier 1: a typical-input test that fires, a clean-ledger silent test, and the acceptance-example tests of the app spec for this detector; each asserts the exact alert count, non-empty source_refs pointing at the right rows, and Alert.detector equal to the registered name.\n4. Tier 2: empty ledger returns [] without raising, single-row ledger returns a list, duplicate source_ref handled, date-window first/last day, and both sides of every numeric threshold constant.\n5. Tier 3: Hypothesis property tests, each with @settings(max_examples=200): no invention, i.e. every Alert.source_refs entry is in loaded_source_refs(ledger, context) (the union of the ledger and every context frame such as suppliers and payments), NOT only in the ledger (CR-LC-3); idempotency; empty input gives []; amounts non-negative; the detector never raises on dirty cells (None, NaN, empty strings, odd types).\n6. Purity: the detector never reads the clock (no date.today, datetime.now, time.time; the as_of date comes from context) and has no I/O or global state mutation.\n7. Thresholds: every threshold is a named UPPER_SNAKE_CASE constant at the top of the module with a business-meaning comment (finance-rules Rule 7), and each is tested on both sides of its boundary.\n\nFor any missing test, write it in the existing test module (or create it), following the patterns, fixtures and builders already in the app's tests/ folder and .kiro/steering/testing.md, with synthetic data only. Do not edit application code; if the detector itself has a defect, describe it in the report instead of fixing it. Finish with a short report (checked / gaps / tests added) and tell the developer to run: pytest apps/<app>/tests/test_<prefix>_<module>.py (substituting the real path), since you cannot assume the tests were executed."
  }
}
